      "math_academy_id": "q-178160",
      "sequence_position": 19,
      "problem": "$$\n{{\\{1,2\\}\\cup \\{3\\}=\\{1,2,3\\}}_{⏟}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{0\\in Z}}\\,\\overset{∧}{\\overset{⏞}{\\text{and}}}\\,\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{1\\text{ is positive}}}}_{⏟}}_{Q\\,∧\\,R}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $P$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $Q∧R$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $P∧(Q∧R)$ is {{field-3}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $P$ is true, $Q$ is true, and $R$ is true. Therefore, $Q∧R$ is true, and the result is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P∧(Q∧R) & ≡\\text{true}∧\\overset{\\text{true}}{\\overset{⏞}{(\\text{true}∧\\text{true})}} \\\\  & ≡\\text{true}∧\\text{true} \\\\  & ≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
